Flaming Sword conjures a blade of pure fire to slash at your enemy. The
sword materializes, strikes once with searing heat, and then dissipates.
Damage scales with the caster's power and can be substantial.

A critical success creates an intensely hot blade that deals double damage.
However, failure to properly control the conjuration can result in the
caster fumbling the flaming blade and stabbing themselves in the foot.

This spell requires a component and cannot be cast underwater, where the
flames would be instantly extinguished. It is considered a tasked spell,
requiring concentration over multiple rounds to complete the casting.

